          "end": 3.27,
          "en": "Instructor: In this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.27,
          "end": 5.04,
          "en": "you'll learn about two ways of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.04,
          "end": 7.17,
          "en": "creating a component dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.17,
          "end": 9.96,
          "en": "The simpler approach is by using NGF",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.96,
          "end": 11.13,
          "en": "and as I mentioned already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.13,
          "end": 14.73,
          "en": "I recommend using that approach as often as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.73,
          "end": 17.94,
          "en": "If you have no strong reason for managing this in code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.94,
          "end": 20.28,
          "en": "for example, you're creating a third-party library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.28,
          "end": 22.32,
          "en": "and want to give users of your library an",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.32,
          "end": 24.09,
          "en": "in-code way of showing an alert,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.09,
          "end": 25.32,
          "en": "that would be a good reason.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 25.32,
          "end": 27.06,
          "en": "But if you have no strong reason,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 27.06,
          "end": 28.2,
          "en": "definitely consider this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 28.2,
          "end": 30.09,
          "en": "It's way easier and Angular does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 30.09,
          "end": 31.74,
          "en": "all the heavy lifting for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 31.74,
          "end": 34.47,
          "en": "And remember, this doesn't render anything in a DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 34.47,
          "end": 35.88,
          "en": "if this condition here is false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 35.88,
          "end": 38.16,
          "en": "So you're also not cluttering your DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 38.16,
          "end": 40.41,
          "en": "with unused or unnecessary content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 40.41,
          "end": 42.576,
          "en": "So strongly consider using NGF.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 42.576,
          "end": 45.21,
          "en": "But if you've got another use case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 45.21,
          "end": 48.24,
          "en": "or you absolutely just want to do it programmatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 48.24,
          "end": 49.59,
          "en": "this is how you do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 49.59,
          "end": 51.57,
          "en": "You create your own component factory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 51.57,
          "end": 53.82,
          "en": "and then you use a view container reference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 53.82,
          "end": 55.74,
          "en": "which you can get access to with the help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 55.74,
          "end": 58.23,
          "en": "of a helper directive, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 58.23,
          "end": 61.53,
          "en": "You use that to then dynamically create and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 61.53,
          "end": 64.77,
          "en": "render your component with the help of Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 64.77,
          "end": 66.57,
          "en": "Important for that approach is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 66.57,
          "end": 68.976,
          "en": "any component you are rendering like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 68.976,
          "end": 71.85,
          "en": "needs to be added to the entry components array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 71.85,
          "end": 74.465,
          "en": "in your module. In your NG module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 74.465,
          "end": 77.376,
          "en": "Otherwise, you will get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 77.376,
          "end": 79.56,
          "en": "Now, these are two different approaches.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 79.56,
          "end": 82.803,
